  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When touching another player's avatar haptics only play on initial touch, cranking sensitivity to max causes haptics to play constantly on collision. Haptics should play when colliding with the outside of an avatar but based on velocity and how far the hand is in the collider. Small movements should have small haptics while large movements should have stronger haptics. But at the same time collision depth should also affect haptic strength.",
